IO-57: count runoff routed onto another subcatchment once in the system runoff

output_saveSubcatchResults() added every subcatchment's runoff to the .out
system "Runoff" (and so to "Total lateral inflow"), including subcatchments
whose outlet is another subcatchment, whose runoff already contains that
runon. Add a subcatchment's runoff only when the runoff mass balance books it
(outlet is a node, or the subcatchment itself), as subcatch_getRunoff() does.
Projects without subcatchment-to-subcatchment routing are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-57_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/output.c b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
index f57370e..6372ac0 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/output.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
@@ -617,7 +617,9 @@ void output_saveSubcatchResults(double reportTime, FILE* file)
             (REAL4)(Subcatch[j].groundwater->evapLoss * UCF(EVAPRATE) * area);
         SysResults[SYS_INFIL] +=
             (REAL4)(SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_INFIL] * area);
-        SysResults[SYS_RUNOFF] += (REAL4)SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_RUNOFF];
+        // --- runoff sent onto another subcatchment is counted there
+        if ( Subcatch[j].outNode >= 0 || Subcatch[j].outSubcatch == j )
+            SysResults[SYS_RUNOFF] += (REAL4)SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_RUNOFF];
     }
 
     // --- normalize system-wide results to catchment area
